LOCATION:San Francisco AIDS Foundation\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/29/el-grupo-de-apoyo-latino-ticket
 s
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Home on Film: A Shorts Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17921240@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:LGBTQ
DESCRIPTION:LOCATION\n\nGLBT Historical Society Museum\n\n4127 18th Street
 \n\nSan Francisco\, CA 94114\n\nADMISSION\n\n$10\; Free for GLBT Historica
 l Society Members\n\nRSVP and reserve your tickets here\n\nThe GLBT Histor
 ical Society presents a screening of short films and archival footage that
  highlight the beauty\, grief\, joy\, and community found in the spaces qu
 eer and trans people call home. In conjunction with the current exhibition
 \, Where We Made Room\, the program will showcase films and footage center
 ed upon the thesis of queer space and carving out room for ourselves.\n\nT
 he screening will be followed by a discussion between Where We Made Room a
 rtist and curator Aleo Landeta and filmmaker Jenni Olson (575 Castro Stree
 t) on these themes and their work.\n\nImage courtesy of Frameline Distribu
 tion\n\n575 Castro St. (2008) - a film by Jenni Olson\n\n7 min.\n\nA power
 ful elegy from acclaimed queer filmmaker Jenni Olson\, 575 Castro St. reve
 als the play of light and shadow upon the walls of the Castro Camera Store
  set for Gus Van Sant’s Academy Award-winning film Milk as we hear excer
 pts from the audio-cassette that Harvey Milk recorded to be played\, “in
  the event of my death by assassination.”\n\nThe film features Milk’s 
 now legendary line\, “Ya gotta give ‘em hope\,” and his eloquent\, t
 imely\, and timeless denouncement of right-wing anti-LGBTQ hate (calling o
 ut Anita Bryant and California Senator John Briggs). The tape was made in 
 November 1977 (after Milk’s election to the San Francisco Board of Super
 visors\, which...\n\n$10\n\nTickets: https://glbthistory.ticketing.veevart
 app.com/tickets/view/list/film-screening-queer-home-on-film-a-shorts-progr
 am-new-date\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/29/queer-home-on
 -film-a-shorts-program-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7608609;-122.4356584
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34810926/c837aca3-398b-42c0-97c1-ee84ee23e7df.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:GLBT History Museum\, 4127 18th St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/29/queer-home-on-film-a-shorts-pro
 gram-tickets
END:VEVENT
